      "problem": "What is the distance between the points $(4,2)$  and $(4,8)?$",
      "worked_solution": "**Method 1** \n\nWe plot the given points in the coordinate plane.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14217432/assets/66c988b7fede0e97eae46388dd0e57aee2c49a3c185c9a888277da8fefc947ab.png)\n\nThe distance between two points is the length of the line segment that connects them.\n\nFrom the diagram, we see that the length of the segment is $6$ units, so the distance equals $6.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14217432/assets/63f70c20c918dae51ecddc7891a8cbee7c5749720521e62fe26e9bc4e33bb9e6.png)\n\n**Method 2**\n\nWe can find the distance between the two points by finding the distance of each point from the $x$-axis and then subtracting.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14217432/assets/d3693b8c3d07636143b2c77c3bd2645015885b77ec4e8ddffde2e121da0511bc.png)\n\nThe point $(4,8)$ is at a distance of $8$ from the $x$-axis, and the point $(4,2)$ is at a distance of $2$ from the $x$-axis. Therefore, the distance between the two points is $8-2=6.$",
